      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <float.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    // Count total points across all groups\n    long total_points = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        total_points += groups[i].length;\n    }\n\n    // Flatten: store label and point for each input point in original order\n    typedef struct { char label; Point p; } LabeledPoint;\n    LabeledPoint *all_pts = (LabeledPoint *)malloc(total_points * sizeof(LabeledPoint));\n    long idx = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            all_pts[idx].label = g.label;\n            all_pts[idx].p = g.points[j];\n            idx++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Determine number of threads and allocate per-thread top-k arrays\n    int nthreads;\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        #pragma omp single\n        nthreads = omp_get_num_threads();\n    }\n\n    char **local_labels = (char**)malloc(nthreads * sizeof(char*));\n    float **local_distances = (float**)malloc(nthreads * sizeof(float*));\n    for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) {\n        local_labels[t] = (char*)malloc(k * sizeof(char));\n        local_distances[t] = (float*)malloc(k * sizeof(float));\n        // Initialize with sentinel values\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            local_labels[t][i] = -1;\n            local_distances[t][i] = -1.0f;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Parallel loop over flattened points, static schedule preserves global order\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (long idx2 = 0; idx2 < total_points; idx2++) {\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        char *llabels = local_labels[tid];\n        float *ldists = local_distances[tid];\n\n        Point p = all_pts[idx2].p;\n        char label = all_pts[idx2].label;\n        float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, p);\n\n        // Early skip: if distance is not better than current k-th best (if already full)\n        if (k > 0 && ldists[k-1] != -1.0f && d >= ldists[k-1]) {\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        // Insert into sorted local top-k array\n        for (int x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n            if (d < ldists[x] || ldists[x] == -1.0f) {\n                // Shift elements to make room\n                for (int y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                    ldists[y] = ldists[y-1];\n                    llabels[y] = llabels[y-1];\n                }\n                ldists[x] = d;\n                llabels[x] = label;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Merge per-thread top-k arrays into global array, preserving original order\n    char *final_labels = (char*)malloc(k * sizeof(char));\n    float *final_distances = (float*)malloc(k * sizeof(float));\n    int *thread_idx = (int*)calloc(nthreads, sizeof(int)); // how many taken from each thread so far\n\n    for (int pos = 0; pos < k; pos++) {\n        int best_tid = -1;\n        float best_d = FLT_MAX;\n        for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) {\n            if (thread_idx[t] < k && local_distances[t][thread_idx[t]] != -1.0f) {\n                float d = local_distances[t][thread_idx[t]];\n                // Tie-break by lower thread ID to preserve original order\n                if (d < best_d || (d == best_d && t < best_tid)) {\n                    best_d = d;\n                    best_tid = t;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if (best_tid == -1) break; // should not happen with valid input\n        final_distances[pos] = local_distances[best_tid][thread_idx[best_tid]];\n        final_labels[pos] = local_labels[best_tid][thread_idx[best_tid]];\n        thread_idx[best_tid]++;\n    }\n\n    // Free per-thread arrays and flattened points (not strictly necessary but good practice)\n    for (int t = 0; t < nthreads; t++) {\n        free(local_labels[t]);\n        free(local_distances[t]);\n    }\n    free(local_labels);\n    free(local_distances);\n    free(thread_idx);\n    free(all_pts);\n\n    // Determine most frequent label among the k nearest neighbors (same as original)\n    qsort(final_labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = final_labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (final_labels[i] != final_labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = final_labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = final_labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(final_labels);\n    free(final_distances);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using OpenMP parallel for with static scheduling on a flattened point array ensures balanced load and preserves global ordering by contiguous chunk assignment. Per-thread local top-k arrays avoid synchronization, and a linear merge in thread ID order with tie-breaking maintains deterministic behavior. Early exit when distance >= current worst reduces insertion overhead.",
  "notes": "Replaced nested group-point loops with a single flattened loop over all points to enable static scheduling on equal-cost iterations. Added early skip for distances not improving the k-th best. Merged per-thread top-k arrays linearly, respecting original order via thread ID tie-breaking when distances are equal.",
